# Deck / Configurator / SLA report

Static front end served by nginx on `:8080`. There is **no build step, no
bundler, no npm, no framework**. Each page is a self-contained HTML file with
inline `<style>` and `<script>`, plus a couple of shared `.js` files.

- `perf-report.html` — SLA & Service Performance Report (portfolio + per-account)
- `QBR Configurator.dc.html` — pulls from the sidecar, edits payload, exports JSON
- `QBR Template*.dc.html`, `index.html`, `deck-stage.js`, `support.js` — the deck

## Hard constraints

- **No runtime network calls to third parties.** No CDN scripts, no Google
  Fonts, no analytics. Fonts are self-hosted under `assets/` (see
  `scripts/fetch-fonts.sh`). This deck gets shown to customers on untrusted
  networks and must render fully offline.
- **Vanilla ES2020.** No TypeScript, no JSX, no imports from a package
  registry.
- Only the sidecar on `:8081` is a legitimate fetch target, and every page must
  still render when it is unreachable.

## The accounts JSON contract

`perf-report.html` discovers `accounts/*.json` through nginx `autoindex` and
parses whatever it finds. Those files are produced by `sf-sync`, so treat the
payload as an external contract:

- Every field may be missing, `null`, or a different type than expected. Guard
  before arithmetic; never let one malformed account blank the whole report.
- SLA rows live in `sourceReview.ticketDetail[]` and carry `openedAs`,
  `slaBound`, `slaBreach`, `slaTargetMins`, `slaActualMins`, `slaMilestone`.
- Severity buckets are driven by **severity at open** (`openedAs`), not the
  case's current severity.
- Percentages are computed over SLA-bound cases only. Cases with
  `slaBound: false` are excluded from both numerator and denominator.

If you change the shape of anything under `sourceReview`, the corresponding
mapping in `sf-sync/mirantis.py` changes in the same pass.

## Configurator specifics

- Never backfill demo data (the Vertex Logistics / Meridian fixtures) into
  fields left blank by a Salesforce pull. Blank means blank, and the
  placeholder banner is what surfaces it.
- Drafts persist in `localStorage`; nothing is written server-side unless the
  user explicitly downloads JSON.
- Sections that Salesforce cannot fill (wins, asks, roadmap, training
  narrative) stay TAM-owned — don't invent generated content for them.

## Style

Match the surrounding file. These are long single-file pages with a consistent
internal idiom; follow the local naming and helper conventions rather than
introducing a new pattern in one section.
